<p><a id=3D"s2.9-generators"></a>
<a id=3D"29-generators"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"generators"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"29-generators">2.9 Generators<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"=
https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#29-generators" aria-label=
=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorj=
s-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>Use generators as needed.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.9.1-definition"></a>
<a id=3D"291-definition"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"generators-definition"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"291-definition">2.9.1 Definition<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=
=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#291-definition" aria-l=
abel=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anc=
horjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>A generator function returns an iterator that yields a value each time i=
t
executes a yield statement. After it yields a value, the runtime state of t=
he
generator function is suspended until the next value is needed.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.9.2-pros"></a>
<a id=3D"292-pros"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"generators-pros"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"292-pros">2.9.2 Pros<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://g=
oogle.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#292-pros" aria-label=3D"Anchor" dat=
a-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; paddin=
g-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Simpler code, because the state of local variables and control flow are
preserved for each call. A generator uses less memory than a function that
creates an entire list of values at once.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.9.3-cons"></a>
<a id=3D"293-cons"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"generators-cons"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"293-cons">2.9.3 Cons<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://g=
oogle.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#293-cons" aria-label=3D"Anchor" dat=
a-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; paddin=
g-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Local variables in the generator will not be garbage collected until the
generator is either consumed to exhaustion or itself garbage collected.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.9.4-decision"></a>
<a id=3D"294-decision"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"generators-decision"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"294-decision">2.9.4 Decision<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"h=
ttps://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#294-decision" aria-label=3D=
"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-i=
cons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Fine. Use =E2=80=9CYields:=E2=80=9D rather than =E2=80=9CReturns:=E2=80=
=9D in the docstring for generator
functions.</p>

<p>If the generator manages an expensive resource, make sure to force the c=
lean up.</p>

<p>A good way to do the clean up is by wrapping the generator with a contex=
t
manager <a href=3D"https://peps.python.org/pep-0533/">PEP-0533</a>.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.10-lambda-functions"></a>
<a id=3D"210-lambda-functions"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"lambdas"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"210-lambda-functions">2.10 Lambda Functions<a class=3D"anchorjs-l=
ink " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#210-lambda-f=
unctions" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"f=
ont: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>Okay for one-liners. Prefer generator expressions over <code class=3D"la=
nguage-plaintext highlighter-rouge">map()</code> or <code class=3D"language=
-plaintext highlighter-rouge">filter()</code>
with a <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">lambda</code>.<=
/p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.10.1-definition"></a>
<a id=3D"2101-definition"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"lambdas-definition"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2101-definition">2.10.1 Definition<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " hre=
f=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2101-definition" aria=
-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 a=
nchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Lambdas define anonymous functions in an expression, as opposed to a sta=
tement.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.10.2-pros"></a>
<a id=3D"2102-pros"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"lambdas-pros"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2102-pros">2.10.2 Pros<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2102-pros" aria-label=3D"Anchor" =
data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; pad=
ding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Convenient.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.10.3-cons"></a>
<a id=3D"2103-cons"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"lambdas-cons"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2103-cons">2.10.3 Cons<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2103-cons" aria-label=3D"Anchor" =
data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; pad=
ding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Harder to read and debug than local functions. The lack of names means s=
tack
traces are more difficult to understand. Expressiveness is limited because =
the
function may only contain an expression.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.10.4-decision"></a>
<a id=3D"2104-decision"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"lambdas-decision"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2104-decision">2.10.4 Decision<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D=
"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2104-decision" aria-label=
=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorj=
s-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Lambdas are allowed. If the code inside the lambda function spans multip=
le lines
or is longer than 60-80 chars, it might be better to define it as a regular
<a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#lexical-scoping=
">nested function</a>.</p>

<p>For common operations like multiplication, use the functions from the <c=
ode class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">operator</code>
module instead of lambda functions. For example, prefer <code class=3D"lang=
uage-plaintext highlighter-rouge">operator.mul</code> to
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">lambda x, y: x * y</co=
de>.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.11-conditional-expressions"></a>
<a id=3D"211-conditional-expressions"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"conditional-expressions"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"211-conditional-expressions">2.11 Conditional Expressions<a class=
=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.htm=
l#211-conditional-expressions" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=
=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"><=
/a></h3>

<p>Okay for simple cases.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.11.1-definition"></a>
<a id=3D"2111-definition"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"conditional-expressions-definition"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2111-definition">2.11.1 Definition<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " hre=
f=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2111-definition" aria=
-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 a=
nchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Conditional expressions (sometimes called a =E2=80=9Cternary operator=E2=
=80=9D) are mechanisms
that provide a shorter syntax for if statements. For example: <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">x =3D 1 if cond
else 2</code>.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.11.2-pros"></a>
<a id=3D"2112-pros"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"conditional-expressions-pros"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2112-pros">2.11.2 Pros<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2112-pros" aria-label=3D"Anchor" =
data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; pad=
ding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Shorter and more convenient than an if statement.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.11.3-cons"></a>
<a id=3D"2113-cons"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"conditional-expressions-cons"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2113-cons">2.11.3 Cons<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2113-cons" aria-label=3D"Anchor" =
data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; pad=
ding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>May be harder to read than an if statement. The condition may be difficu=
lt to
locate if the expression is long.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.11.4-decision"></a>
<a id=3D"2114-decision"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"conditional-expressions-decision"></a></p>
