<p>Okay in most cases.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.12.1-definition"></a>
<a id=3D"2121-definition"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"default-arguments-definition"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2121-definition">2.12.1 Definition<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " hre=
f=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2121-definition" aria=
-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 a=
nchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>You can specify values for variables at the end of a function=E2=80=99s =
parameter list,
e.g., <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">def foo(a, b=3D0=
):</code>. If <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">foo</cod=
e> is called with only one argument, <code class=3D"language-plaintext high=
lighter-rouge">b</code> is set
to 0. If it is called with two arguments, <code class=3D"language-plaintext=
 highlighter-rouge">b</code> has the value of the second
argument.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.12.2-pros"></a>
<a id=3D"2122-pros"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"default-arguments-pros"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2122-pros">2.12.2 Pros<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2122-pros" aria-label=3D"Anchor" =
data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; pad=
ding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Often you have a function that uses lots of default values, but on rare
occasions you want to override the defaults. Default argument values provid=
e an
easy way to do this, without having to define lots of functions for the rar=
e
exceptions. As Python does not support overloaded methods/functions, defaul=
t
arguments are an easy way of =E2=80=9Cfaking=E2=80=9D the overloading behav=
ior.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.12.3-cons"></a>
<a id=3D"2123-cons"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"default-arguments-cons"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"2123-cons">2.12.3 Cons<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#2123-cons" aria-label=3D"Anchor" =
data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; pad=
ding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Default arguments are evaluated once at module load time. This may cause
problems if the argument is a mutable object such as a list or a dictionary=
. If
the function modifies the object (e.g., by appending an item to a list), th=
e
default value is modified.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s2.12.4-decision"></a>
<a id=3D"2124-decision"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"default-arguments-decision"></a></p>
