<h4 id=3D"341-trailing-commas-in-sequences-of-items">3.4.1 Trailing commas =
in sequences of items?<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://google.gi=
thub.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#341-trailing-commas-in-sequences-of-items" =
aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em /=
 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Trailing commas in sequences of items are recommended only when the clos=
ing
container token <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">]</cod=
e>, <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">)</code>, or <code=
 class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">}</code> does not appear on=
 the same line as the final
element, as well as for tuples with a single element. The presence of a tra=
iling
comma is also used as a hint to our Python code auto-formatter
<a href=3D"https://github.com/psf/black">Black</a> or <a href=3D"https://gi=
thub.com/google/pyink">Pyink</a>
to direct it to auto-format the container of items to one item per line whe=
n the
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">,</code> after the fin=
al element is present.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"p"=
>:</span>   <span class=3D"n">golomb3</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <=
