<p>A method that overrides a method from a base class does not need a docst=
ring if
it is explicitly decorated with
<a href=3D"https://typing-extensions.readthedocs.io/en/latest/#override"><c=
ode class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">@override</code></a>
(from <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typing_extension=
s</code> or <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typing</co=
de> modules), unless the overriding method=E2=80=99s
behavior materially refines the base method=E2=80=99s contract, or details =
need to be
provided (e.g., documenting additional side effects), in which case a docst=
ring
with at least those differences is required on the overriding method.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">from</span> <span class=3D=
"nn">typing_extensions</span> <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=
=3D"n">override</span>

<span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">Parent</span><span class=
=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">do_something</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">):</spa=
n>
    <span class=3D"s">"""Parent method, includes docstring."""</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Child class, method annotated with override.
</span><span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">Child</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">Parent</span><span class=3D"p">):</sp=
an>
  <span class=3D"o">@</span><span class=3D"n">override</span>
  <span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">do_something</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">):</spa=
n>
    <span class=3D"k">pass</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1"># Child class, but without=
 @override decorator, a docstring is required.
</span><span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">Child</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">Parent</span><span class=3D"p">):</sp=
an>
  <span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">do_something</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">):</spa=
n>
    <span class=3D"k">pass</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Docstring is trivial, @override is sufficient to indic=
ate that docs can be
# found in the base class.
</span><span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">Child</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">Parent</span><span class=3D"p">):</sp=
an>
  <span class=3D"o">@</span><span class=3D"n">override</span>
  <span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">do_something</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">):</spa=
n>
    <span class=3D"s">"""See base class."""</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><a id=3D"s3.8.4-comments-in-classes"></a>
<a id=3D"384-classes"></a>
<a id=3D"comments-in-classes"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"class-docs"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"384-classes">3.8.4 Classes<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"htt=
ps://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#384-classes" aria-label=3D"An=
chor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icon=
s; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Classes should have a docstring below the class definition describing th=
e class.
Public attributes, excluding <a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide=
/pyguide.html#properties">properties</a>, should be documented
here in an <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Attributes<=
/code> section and follow the same formatting as a
<a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#doc-function-ar=
gs">function=E2=80=99s <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"=
>Args</code></a> section.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D=
"nc">SampleClass</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
    <span class=3D"s">"""Summary of class here.

    Longer class information...
    Longer class information...

    Attributes:
        likes_spam: A boolean indicating if we like SPAM or not.
        eggs: An integer count of the eggs we have laid.
    """</span>

    <span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">__init__</span><span cl=
ass=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> =
<span class=3D"n">likes_spam</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=
=3D"nb">bool</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"bp">False</=
span><span class=3D"p">):</span>
        <span class=3D"s">"""Initializes the instance based on spam prefere=
nce.

        Args:
          likes_spam: Defines if instance exhibits this preference.
        """</span>
        <span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=
=3D"n">likes_spam</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">lik=
es_spam</span>
        <span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=
=3D"n">eggs</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"mi">0</span>

    <span class=3D"o">@</span><span class=3D"nb">property</span>
    <span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">butter_sticks</span><sp=
an class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"bp">self</span><span class=3D"p">)</s=
pan> <span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"nb">int</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">:</span>
        <span class=3D"s">"""The number of butter sticks we have."""</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>All class docstrings should start with a one-line summary that describes=
 what
the class instance represents. This implies that subclasses of <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Exception</code>
should also describe what the exception represents, and not the context in =
which
it might occur. The class docstring should not repeat unnecessary informati=
on,
such as that the class is a class.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1"># Yes:
</span><span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">CheeseShopAddress<=
/span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"s">"""The address of a cheese shop.

  ...
  """</span>

<span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">OutOfCheeseError</span><s=
pan class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"nb">Exception</span><span class=3D"p=
">):</span>
  <span class=3D"s">"""No more cheese is available."""</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1"># No:
</span><span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">CheeseShopAddress<=
/span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"s">"""Class that describes the address of a cheese shop.

  ...
  """</span>

<span class=3D"k">class</span> <span class=3D"nc">OutOfCheeseError</span><s=
pan class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"nb">Exception</span><span class=3D"p=
">):</span>
  <span class=3D"s">"""Raised when no more cheese is available."""</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><a id=3D"s3.8.5-block-and-inline-comments"></a>
