<p><a id=3D"comments"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"385-block-and-inline-comments">3.8.5 Block and Inline Comments<a =
class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguid=
e.html#385-block-and-inline-comments" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-i=
con=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.37=
5em;"></a></h4>

<p>The final place to have comments is in tricky parts of the code. If you=
=E2=80=99re going
to have to explain it at the next <a href=3D"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C=
ode_review">code review</a>,
you should comment it now. Complicated operations get a few lines of commen=
ts
before the operations commence. Non-obvious ones get comments at the end of=
 the
line.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1"># We use a weighted dictio=
nary search to find out where i is in
# the array.  We extrapolate position based on the largest num
# in the array and the array size and then do binary search to
# get the exact number.
</span>
<span class=3D"k">if</span> <span class=3D"n">i</span> <span class=3D"o">&a=
mp;</span> <span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">i</span><span class=
=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"mi">1</span><span class=3D"p">)</span> <span =
class=3D"o">=3D=3D</span> <span class=3D"mi">0</span><span class=3D"p">:</s=
pan>  <span class=3D"c1"># True if i is 0 or a power of 2.
</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p>To improve legibility, these comments should start at least 2 spaces awa=
y from
the code with the comment character <code class=3D"language-plaintext highl=
ighter-rouge">#</code>, followed by at least one space before
the text of the comment itself.</p>

<p>On the other hand, never describe the code. Assume the person reading th=
e code
knows Python (though not what you=E2=80=99re trying to do) better than you =
do.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1"># BAD COMMENT: Now go thro=
ugh the b array and make sure whenever i occurs
# the next element is i+1
</span></code></pre></div></div>

