<p><a id=3D"strings"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"310-strings">3.10 Strings<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"http=
s://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#310-strings" aria-label=3D"Anc=
hor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons=
; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>Use an
<a href=3D"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#f-stri=
ngs">f-string</a>,
the <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">%</code> operator,=
 or the <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">format</code> =
method for formatting strings, even when the
parameters are all strings. Use your best judgment to decide between string
formatting options. A single join with <code class=3D"language-plaintext hi=
ghlighter-rouge">+</code> is okay but do not format with <code class=3D"lan=
guage-plaintext highlighter-rouge">+</code>.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"p"=
>:</span> <span class=3D"n">x</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"sa">f</span><span class=3D"s">'name: </span><span class=3D"si">{</spa=
n><span class=3D"n">name</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s"=
>; score: </span><span class=3D"si">{</span><span class=3D"n">n</span><span=
 class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s">'</span>
     <span class=3D"n">x</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D=
"s">'%s, %s!'</span> <span class=3D"o">%</span> <span class=3D"p">(</span><=
span class=3D"n">imperative</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D=
"n">expletive</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
