<p>Be consistent with your choice of string quote character within a file. =
Pick <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">'</code>
or <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"</code> and stick =
with it. It is okay to use the other quote character on a
string to avoid the need to backslash-escape quote characters within the st=
ring.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"p"=
>:</span>
  <span class=3D"n">Python</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s=
">'Why are you hiding your eyes?'</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
  <span class=3D"n">Gollum</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s=
">"I'm scared of lint errors."</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
  <span class=3D"n">Narrator</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D=
"s">'"Good!" thought a happy Python reviewer.'</span><span class=3D"p">)</s=
pan>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">No</span><span class=3D"p">=
:</span>
  <span class=3D"n">Python</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s=
">"Why are you hiding your eyes?"</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
  <span class=3D"n">Gollum</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s=
">'The lint. It burns. It burns us.'</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
  <span class=3D"n">Gollum</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s=
">"Always the great lint. Watching. Watching."</span><span class=3D"p">)</s=
pan>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Prefer <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"""</code> f=
or multi-line strings rather than <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlig=
hter-rouge">'''</code>. Projects may choose to
use <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">'''</code> for all=
 non-docstring multi-line strings if and only if they also use
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">'</code> for regular s=
trings. Docstrings must use <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-r=
ouge">"""</code> regardless.</p>

<p>Multi-line strings do not flow with the indentation of the rest of the p=
rogram.
If you need to avoid embedding extra space in the string, use either
concatenated single-line strings or a multi-line string with
<a href=3D"https://docs.python.org/3/library/textwrap.html#textwrap.dedent"=
><code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">textwrap.dedent()</co=
de></a>
to remove the initial space on each line:</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code>  <span class=3D"n">No</span><span class=3D"p=
">:</span>
  <span class=3D"n">long_string</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span c=
lass=3D"s">"""This is pretty ugly.
Don't do this.
"""</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code>  <span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"=
p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"n">long_string</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span c=
lass=3D"s">"""This is fine if your use case can accept
      extraneous leading spaces."""</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code>  <span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"=
p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"n">long_string</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span c=
lass=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s">"And this is fine if you cannot accept=
</span><span class=3D"se">\n</span><span class=3D"s">"</span> <span class=
=3D"o">+</span>
                 <span class=3D"s">"extraneous leading spaces."</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code>  <span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"=
p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"n">long_string</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span c=
lass=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s">"And this too is fine if you cannot ac=
cept</span><span class=3D"se">\n</span><span class=3D"s">"</span>
                 <span class=3D"s">"extraneous leading spaces."</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code>  <span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"=
p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">textwrap</span>

  <span class=3D"n">long_string</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span c=
lass=3D"n">textwrap</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">deden=
t</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s">"""</span><span class=
=3D"se">\
</span><span class=3D"s">      This is also fine, because textwrap.dedent()
      will collapse common leading spaces in each line."""</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Note that using a backslash here does not violate the prohibition agains=
t
<a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#line-length">ex=
plicit line continuation</a>; in this case, the backslash is
<a href=3D"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#string=
-and-bytes-literals">escaping a newline</a>
in a string literal.</p>

