<h4 id=3D"3195-nonetype">3.19.5 NoneType<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D=
"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#3195-nonetype" aria-label=
=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorj=
s-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>In the Python type system, <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter=
-rouge">NoneType</code> is a =E2=80=9Cfirst class=E2=80=9D type, and for ty=
ping
purposes, <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">None</code> =
is an alias for <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NoneTy=
pe</code>. If an argument can be <code class=3D"language-plaintext highligh=
ter-rouge">None</code>, it
has to be declared! You can use <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlight=
er-rouge">|</code> union type expressions (recommended in new
Python 3.10+ code), or the older <code class=3D"language-plaintext highligh=
ter-rouge">Optional</code> and <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighte=
r-rouge">Union</code> syntaxes.</p>

<p>Use explicit <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">X | No=
ne</code> instead of implicit. Earlier versions of PEP 484 allowed
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">a: str =3D None</code>=
 to be interpreted as <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">=
a: str | None =3D None</code>, but that is no
longer the preferred behavior.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">Yes</span><span class=3D"p"=
>:</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">modern_or_union</span><span=
 class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">a</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <=
span class=3D"nb">str</span> <span class=3D"o">|</span> <span class=3D"nb">=
int</span> <span class=3D"o">|</span> <span class=3D"bp">None</span><span c=
lass=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">b</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <s=
pan class=3D"nb">str</span> <span class=3D"o">|</span> <span class=3D"bp">N=
one</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"bp">None</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span> <span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"nb">str=
</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"p">...</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">union_optional</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">a</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <s=
pan class=3D"n">Union</span><span class=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"nb">st=
r</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"nb">int</span><span class=
=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"bp">None</span><span class=3D"p">],</span> <=
span class=3D"n">b</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=3D"n">Optio=
nal</span><span class=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"nb">str</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">]</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"bp">None</span=
><span class=3D"p">)</span> <span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"n=
b">str</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"p">...</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">No</span><span class=3D"p">=
:</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">nullable_union</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">a</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <s=
pan class=3D"n">Union</span><span class=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"bp">No=
ne</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"nb">str</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">])</span> <span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"nb">str</sp=
an><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"p">...</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">implicit_optional</span><sp=
an class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">a</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>=
 <span class=3D"nb">str</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"=
bp">None</span><span class=3D"p">)</span> <span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <s=
pan class=3D"nb">str</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
