</p>

<p>Note that the <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">: Typ=
eAlias</code> annotation is only supported in versions 3.10+.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">from</span> <span class=3D=
"nn">typing</span> <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"n">TypeA=
lias</span>

<span class=3D"n">_LossAndGradient</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span c=
lass=3D"n">TypeAlias</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"nb"=
>tuple</span><span class=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"n">tf</span><span cla=
ss=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">Tensor</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> =
<span class=3D"n">tf</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">Tens=
or</span><span class=3D"p">]</span>
<span class=3D"n">ComplexTFMap</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=
=3D"n">TypeAlias</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">Mapp=
ing</span><span class=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"nb">str</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">_LossAndGradient</span><span class=3D"p"=
>]</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><a id=3D"s3.19.7-ignoring-types"></a>
<a id=3D"s3.19.7-ignore"></a>
<a id=3D"3197-ignoring-types"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-ignore"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"3197-ignoring-types">3.19.7 Ignoring Types<a class=3D"anchorjs-li=
nk " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#3197-ignoring=
-types" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"fon=
t: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>You can disable type checking on a line with the special comment <code c=
lass=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"># type:
ignore</code>.</p>

<p><code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pytype</code> has a=
 disable option for specific errors (similar to lint):</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1"># pytype: disable=3Dattrib=
ute-error
</span></code></pre></div></div>

<p><a id=3D"s3.19.8-typing-variables"></a>
<a id=3D"s3.19.8-comments"></a>
<a id=3D"3198-typing-internal-variables"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-variables"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"3198-typing-variables">3.19.8 Typing Variables<a class=3D"anchorj=
s-link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#3198-typi=
ng-variables" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=
=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<dl>
  <dt><a id=3D"annotated-assignments"></a></dt>
  <dt><a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#annotated=
-assignments"><em>Annotated Assignments</em></a></dt>
  <dd>If an internal variable has a type that is hard or impossible to infe=
r,
specify its type with an annotated assignment - use a colon and type betwee=
n
the variable name and value (the same as is done with function arguments
that have a default value):

    <div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highligh=
t"><pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">a</span><span class=3D"=
p">:</span> <span class=3D"n">Foo</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span=
 class=3D"n">SomeUndecoratedFunction</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
</code></pre></div>    </div>
  </dd>
  <dt><a id=3D"type-comments"></a></dt>
  <dt><a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#type-comm=
ents"><em>Type Comments</em></a></dt>
  <dd>Though you may see them remaining in the codebase (they were necessar=
y
before Python 3.6), do not add any more uses of a <code class=3D"language-p=
laintext highlighter-rouge"># type: &lt;type name&gt;</code>
comment on the end of the line:

    <div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highligh=
t"><pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">a</span> <span class=3D=
"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">SomeUndecoratedFunction</span><span class=
=3D"p">()</span>  <span class=3D"c1"># type: Foo
</span></code></pre></div>    </div>
  </dd>
</dl>

<p><a id=3D"s3.19.9-tuples-vs-lists"></a>
<a id=3D"s3.19.9-tuples"></a>
<a id=3D"3199-tuples-vs-lists"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-tuples"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"3199-tuples-vs-lists">3.19.9 Tuples vs Lists<a class=3D"anchorjs-=
link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#3199-tuples=
-vs-lists" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"=
font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>Typed lists can only contain objects of a single type. Typed tuples can =
either
have a single repeated type or a set number of elements with different type=
s.
The latter is commonly used as the return type from a function.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"n">a</span><span class=3D"p">:=
