<p>A common predefined type variable in the <code class=3D"language-plainte=
xt highlighter-rouge">typing</code> module is <code class=3D"language-plain=
text highlighter-rouge">AnyStr</code>. Use it for
multiple annotations that can be <code class=3D"language-plaintext highligh=
ter-rouge">bytes</code> or <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-ro=
uge">str</code> and must all be the same type.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">from</span> <span class=3D=
"nn">typing</span> <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"n">AnySt=
r</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">check_length</span><span cl=
ass=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <spa=
n class=3D"n">AnyStr</span><span class=3D"p">)</span> <span class=3D"o">-&g=
t;</span> <span class=3D"n">AnyStr</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"k">if</span> <span class=3D"nb">len</span><span class=3D"p=
">(</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=3D"p">)</span> <span class=
=3D"o">&lt;=3D</span> <span class=3D"mi">42</span><span class=3D"p">:</span=
>
    <span class=3D"k">return</span> <span class=3D"n">x</span>
  <span class=3D"k">raise</span> <span class=3D"nb">ValueError</span><span =
class=3D"p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

