<p><a id=3D"s3.19.11-string-types"></a>
<a id=3D"s3.19.11-strings"></a>
<a id=3D"31911-string-types"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-strings"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"31911-string-types">3.19.11 String types<a class=3D"anchorjs-link=
 " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#31911-string-ty=
pes" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: =
1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<blockquote>
  <p>Do not use <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typing=
.Text</code> in new code. It=E2=80=99s only for Python 2/3 compatibility.</=
p>
</blockquote>

<p>Use <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">str</code> for =
string/text data. For code that deals with binary data, use
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">bytes</code>.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"n=
f">deals_with_text_data</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x=
</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=3D"nb">str</span><span class=
=3D"p">)</span> <span class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"nb">str</span=
><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"p">...</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">deals_with_binary_data</spa=
n><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=3D"p">:</=
span> <span class=3D"nb">bytes</span><span class=3D"p">)</span> <span class=
=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"nb">bytes</span><span class=3D"p">:</spa=
n>
  <span class=3D"p">...</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>If all the string types of a function are always the same, for example i=
f the
return type is the same as the argument type in the code above, use
<a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#typing-type-var=
">AnyStr</a>.</p>

<p><a id=3D"s3.19.12-imports-for-typing"></a>
<a id=3D"s3.19.12-imports"></a>
<a id=3D"31912-imports-for-typing"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-imports"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"31912-imports-for-typing">3.19.12 Imports For Typing<a class=3D"a=
nchorjs-link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#319=
12-imports-for-typing" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=
=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h=
4>

<p>For symbols (including types, functions, and constants) from the <code c=
lass=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typing</code> or
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">collections.abc</code>=
 modules used to support static analysis and type checking,
always import the symbol itself. This keeps common annotations more concise=
 and
matches typing practices used around the world. You are explicitly allowed =
to
import multiple specific symbols on one line from the <code class=3D"langua=
ge-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typing</code> and
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">collections.abc</code>=
 modules. For example:</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">from</span> <span class=3D=
"nn">collections.abc</span> <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D=
"n">Mapping</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">Sequence</sp=
an>
<span class=3D"kn">from</span> <span class=3D"nn">typing</span> <span class=
=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"n">Any</span><span class=3D"p">,</span=
> <span class=3D"n">Generic</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D=
"n">cast</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">TYPE_CHECKING</=
span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Given that this way of importing adds items to the local namespace, name=
s in
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typing</code> or <code=
 class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">collections.abc</code> shou=
ld be treated similarly to keywords, and not
be defined in your Python code, typed or not. If there is a collision betwe=
en a
type and an existing name in a module, import it using <code class=3D"langu=
age-plaintext highlighter-rouge">import x as y</code>.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">from</span> <span class=3D=
"nn">typing</span> <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"n">Any</=
span> <span class=3D"k">as</span> <span class=3D"n">AnyType</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Prefer to use built-in types as annotations where available. Python supp=
orts
type annotations using parametric container types via
<a href=3D"https://peps.python.org/pep-0585/">PEP-585</a>, introduced in Py=
thon 3.9.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"n=
f">generate_foo_scores</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">fo=
o</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=3D"nb">set</span><span class=
=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"nb">str</span><span class=3D"p">])</span> <sp=
an class=3D"o">-&gt;</span> <span class=3D"nb">list</span><span class=3D"p"=
>[</span><span class=3D"nb">float</span><span class=3D"p">]:</span>
  <span class=3D"p">...</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p><a id=3D"s3.19.13-conditional-imports"></a>
<a id=3D"31913-conditional-imports"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-conditional-imports"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"31913-conditional-imports">3.19.13 Conditional Imports<a class=3D=
"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#3=
1913-conditional-imports" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=
=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a>=
</h4>

<p>Use conditional imports only in exceptional cases where the additional i=
mports
needed for type checking must be avoided at runtime. This pattern is
discouraged; alternatives such as refactoring the code to allow top-level
imports should be preferred.</p>

<p>Imports that are needed only for type annotations can be placed within a=
n <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">if
TYPE_CHECKING:</code> block.</p>

<ul>
  <li>Conditionally imported types need to be referenced as strings, to be =
forward
compatible with Python 3.6 where the annotation expressions are actually
evaluated.</li>
  <li>Only entities that are used solely for typing should be defined here;=
 this
includes aliases. Otherwise it will be a runtime error, as the module will
not be imported at runtime.</li>
  <li>The block should be right after all the normal imports.</li>
  <li>There should be no empty lines in the typing imports list.</li>
  <li>Sort this list as if it were a regular imports list.
    <div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highligh=
t"><pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"nn">typing</span>
<span class=3D"k">if</span> <span class=3D"n">typing</span><span class=3D"p=
">.</span><span class=3D"n">TYPE_CHECKING</span><span class=3D"p">:</span>
  <span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">sketch</span>
<span class=3D"k">def</span> <span class=3D"nf">f</span><span class=3D"p">(=
</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=3D"=
s">"sketch.Sketch"</span><span class=3D"p">):</span> <span class=3D"p">...<=
/span>
</code></pre></div>    </div>
  </li>
</ul>

<p><a id=3D"s3.19.14-circular-dependencies"></a>
<a id=3D"s3.19.14-circular-deps"></a>
<a id=3D"31914-circular-dependencies"></a></p>

<p><a id=3D"typing-circular-deps"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"31914-circular-dependencies">3.19.14 Circular Dependencies<a clas=
s=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.ht=
ml#31914-circular-dependencies" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D=
"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;">=
</a></h4>

<p>Circular dependencies that are caused by typing are code smells. Such co=
de is a
good candidate for refactoring. Although technically it is possible to keep
circular dependencies, various build systems will not let you do so
because each module has to depend on the other.</p>

<p>Replace modules that create circular dependency imports with <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Any</code>. Set an
<a href=3D"https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#typing-aliases"=
>alias</a> with a meaningful name, and use the real type name from
this module (any attribute of <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter=
-rouge">Any</code> is <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">=
